  "user_request_original": "Optimize an 18-layer TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate at 45 degree incidence for unpolarized light. Layer sequence: TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2, TiO2, SiO2 (18 layers total, starting with TiO2 at air interface). Initialize thicknesses to [174.47, 201.69, 182.61, 99.19, 166.54, 299.73, 55.42, 91.41, 211.51, 103.06, 173.72, 227.47, 172.37, 74.51, 222.81, 77.31, 205.14, 262.69] nm. Apply asymmetric perturbation bounds during optimization: layers 0, 1, 2, 15, 16, 17 constrained to seed value ±15 nm; layers 3 through 14 constrained to seed value ±30 nm. Optimize for maximum reflectance in 450-650 nm band and maximum transmittance in 700-1000 nm band. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 450-650 nm, 700-1000 nm. soft objectives: high reflectance in 450-650 nm; high transmittance in 700-1000 nm; minimized crosstalk between bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 450-650 nm; reflectance in 700-1000 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 24 layers.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize an 18-layer alternating TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica at 45° incidence for unpolarized light. Enforce high reflectance and low transmittance in 450–650 nm, and high transmittance and low reflectance in 700–1000 nm using gradient-based thickness optimization with seed-centered bounds.",
